# Raw run data IS committed, deliberately.
#
# The original rule here excluded it, on the reasoning that runs are cheap to
# reproduce. That reasoning was wrong twice over: 56 runs of a reasoning model
# cost real money, and this project is now shelved, so they will never be
# reproduced. Every number in docs/REPORT.md comes out of these files -- with
# them the report is auditable down to the individual run, without them it is
# a set of assertions.
#
# The risk the old rule guarded against (quietly amending a published number)
# is better handled by the fact that these files are now in git history: an
# amendment shows up as a diff.

# Per-run workspaces: regenerated fixtures and scratch dirs, not evidence.
/workspaces/

# Captured reference sessions point at absolute paths in one machine's
# $DSH_HOME; another checkout must capture its own.
/reference/reference-manifest.json
/reference/composed-config.yml

node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
